MCP verification against running container
- `initialize` on `http://localhost:15000/mcp` succeeded.
- `tools/list` result did not contain `execute_f_sharp_code_async`.
- `resources/templates/list` result did contain `fsiAsyncStatus`.

Root cause evidence
- `/workspace/home/mcp/csharp-sdk/src/ModelContextProtocol.Core/Server/AIFunctionMcpServerTool.cs:320`
- SDK removes the `Async` suffix from async method names before snake_case conversion.
- Therefore `ExecuteFSharpCodeAsync` derived to `execute_f_sharp_code`, colliding with the existing sync tool.

Build
- Command: `dotnet build FSharp.MCP.DevKit.sln`
- Result: success
- Warnings: existing `NU1510` warnings in `FSharp.MCP.DevKit.Documentation.fsproj`

Local source verification
- Started local server with:
  `ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://127.0.0.1:18080 MCP_ENABLE_STDIO=false dotnet run --project /workspace/home/mcp/FSharp.MCP.DevKit/src/FSharp.MCP.DevKit.Server/FSharp.MCP.DevKit.Server.fsproj --framework net10.0 --no-launch-profile`
- Performed `initialize -> notifications/initialized -> tools/list`
- Verified response now contains:
  - `execute_f_sharp_code`
  - `execute_f_sharp_code_async`
  - `execute_f_sharp_code_detailed`

Deployment note
- The currently running Docker container still serves the old build until rebuilt/restarted.
